    "picture_copyright": "Joseph Kunnappally"
  },
  "comments": "<p>Bombay mintmarks<br>♦ - Circulation strikes<br>B - Proof strikes<br><br>KM#49.1 Type 1 - lion with whiskers, faces and wheel redesigned.<br>KM#49.2 Type 2 - 9 mm between lions' nose tips, 15 mm across field. Bull has three legs.<br>KM#49.3 Type 2 - 10 mm between lion nose tips, 16-16.3 mm across field. Bull has three legs.<br>KM#49.4 Type 1 - central lion with bull and horse re-engraved.<br>KM#49.5 Type 3.<br>KM#49.6 Type 2 - 9-1/2 mm between lions' nose tips. Bull has four legs.<br>KM#49.7 Mule: Obverse of KM#48.2 Nickel issue (Lion face without whiskers) and Reverse of KM#49.1.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/690b9610b9b3a.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/690b9610b9b3a.jpg\"></a></p><p><br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5b59dd976d0e5.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5b59dd976d0e5.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><br>- The center Lion on the KM#49.4 has re-engraved mouth, chest hair and bull and horse (click on image to zoom).<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5b89644c3c881.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5b89644c3c881.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>1988 Calcutta mint details:<br>Obverse: different lions<br>Reverse: wide and narrow date<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5f45c5d9daa45.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5f45c5d9daa45.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>Detail of re-engraving KM#49.7 vs KM#49.1.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/581b2b57a486e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/581b2b57a486e.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>1976B Borders<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62d26ed219ca6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62d26ed219ca6.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p>",
